{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791029563,"nonce":"dzoEMr7Hj/AcxukEK9xn8K8MOx4=","title":"SVG \u003ctext\u003e draws nothing: blinc_svg parses with an empty font database","message":"RasterizedSvg::from_data in blinc_svg (rasterize.rs, and document.rs) uses usvg::Options::default(), whose fontdb is empty, so every \u003ctext\u003e in an SVG renders no pixels, in Blinc as well as ashui. Asked blinc-b1 to keep one process-wide font database in blinc_svg, loaded lazily on the first document with text.\n\nReproducer, which inks zero pixels:\n\n    \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\u003e\u003ctext x=\"0\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"currentColor\"\u003eM\u003c/text\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n\nWhen it lands: add a render probe to tests/fixtures/render/Pixels.hx with this document as another icon in the \"full svg\" row, coloured red by the element, counting red pixels in its 24x24 cell (expect well over 40).","files":null}]}